Z||000000||AZ RED FRED||12-04-2001||01:30 AM||||What I great site this is! I have just recently re-discovered the Fiero. I had owned a 84 SE then got a 86 GT back when they were new. Some where along the way I got side tracked to Hondas, it started with a 89 CRX and the most recent was a 99 Odyssey. A mini van,isn't that pathetic. I knew I needed a change. Well I'm pushing 50 now and needed to get back into something sporty. Looked around at new stuff but couldn't find anything that was "special" that I could afford. Went to a car show one Sat. and there were 3 Fiero's there and then I knew what I had to get. Got a 88 GT Med.Red Met. from an original owner in Ohio. It has 9,500 miles on it. Original everything except the battery. He never even drove it in the rain! So far no problems,its been one month and 425 miles. Any second thoughts I had about owning a 13+ year old car are gone now knowing there is a forum such as this for info and help. ||||reg||1
